    <h1>MwalaJS Framework Help</h1>
    <div class="help-content">
      <p>Available commands for MwalaJS framework:</p>
      <pre>
1. <span class="command">mwala create &lt;appname&gt;</span> - Create a new MVC project. Example: mwala create myapp
2. <span class="command">mwala app.mjs</span> - Run the app.mjs file to start your application.
3. <span class="command">mwala db &lt;command&gt;</span> - Database commands for various database tasks:
    - create-database - Creates a new database.
    - migrate - Run migrations.
    - rollback - Rollback migrations.
4. <span class="command">mwala generate &lt;model/controller/route/view&gt; &lt;name&gt;</span> - Generate various MVC components (models, controllers, routes, and views).
    - Example: mwala generate model user
    - Example: mwala generate controller userController
    - Example: mwala generate route userRoute
    - Example: mwala generate view userView
5. <span class="command">mwala add middleware &lt;middlewareName&gt;</span> - Add a middleware to your project. Example: mwala add middleware auth
6. <span class="command">mwala serve</span> - Start the server (similar to running "mwala app.mjs" or "node app.mjs").
7. <span class="command">mwala help</span> - Show available commands (this command).
8. <span class="command">mwala create-table &lt;table_name&gt;</span> - Create a table in the database. Example: mwala create-table users
9. <span class="command">mwala drop-table &lt;table_name&gt;</span> - Drop a table from the database. Example: mwala drop-table users
10. <span class="command">mwala migrate</span> - Run migrations on the database. Example: mwala migrate
11. <span class="command">mwala rollback</span> - Rollback the last migration. Example: mwala rollback
      </pre>
    </div>
